{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790721908,"nonce":"ns1+ow61C5m6C9mFacOzntwRnac=","title":"Hybrid Thread.create fibers remain on the main interpreter scheduler","message":"Default hybrid mode does not dispatch a cold Haxe thread root to a native worker lane. With ASH_WORKERS=4, four FixedThreadPool(4) worker fibers are installed on the main scheduler even though the worker pool is enabled. ASH_FIBER_TRACE=1 shows four `resolve-failed` events for the same thread-root sentinel (detail=607), then `install id=1..4 detail=1`, and no `dispatch` events. `--jit-log` shows no promotion of that thread root. The same bytecode with ASH_STUB_COMPILE=1 logs `resolve findex=606`, `install findex=606 tier=cranelift`, then `dispatch id=1..4 detail=0..3`. `--mode jit` also dispatches all four.\n\nThe cause is the interaction between ash_std/src/fiber.rs thread_create and crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/mod.rs jit_stub_resolver. thread_create tries to resolve the root's findex+1 sentinel before choosing a worker lane. This call occurs on the main thread. In hybrid mode, jit_stub_resolver returns null for a main-thread cold stub unless ASH_STUB_COMPILE is enabled, so thread_create installs an interpreter fiber on the main scheduler. A FixedThreadPool creates its long-lived worker roots only four times, below the default call-count promotion threshold. Once installed, those fibers remain on the main scheduler.\n\nReproduce using the sibling ChimpMonk checkout: compile a program that constructs FixedThreadPool(4), then for 20 frames submits 16 empty closures and waits on a Lock for all 16 completions. Run ASH_WORKERS=4 ASH_FIBER_TRACE=1 ash --jit-log program.hl, then repeat with ASH_STUB_COMPILE=1 and --mode jit. The committed example/src/ConcurrentWorldChecks.hx uses the same FixedThreadPool pattern with actual physics work; its default hybrid serial-versus-parallel assertion also encounters a separate tier trajectory issue tracked as 30c687547240d726c99aab1bc7c3401f654fe172c27b89a21de1a799bc8dffaa.\n\nCompile thread-root closures at spawn or provide a dedicated resolver path for them so hybrid mode can place worker fibers on native lanes without globally forcing synchronous compilation of every cold callee. AOT already dispatches these fibers, so the separate AOT short-job slowdown is not caused by this issue.","files":null}]}